'' std/containers Map and Set under put/remove churn over distinct keys. Reserve returned early
'' whenever the live count fit, so the tombstones were never dropped: after 8 cycles at capacity
'' 8 no EMPTY slot ended a probe, and every later Put / Add dropped its key and returned FALSE
'' (found by the tiko-lsp document store, which lost documents after ~8 open/close cycles). The
'' fix rehashes at the same size while live entries fill at most half, doubled past that.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 -i toolchains/tiko-windows/inc tests/modules/src/stdfacade/containers-tombstones.bas -o tests/modules/stdcontainerstomb.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/modules/stdcontainerstomb.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: single 0 0 0 8
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: steady 0 5 5 16
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: indexer 0 0 8
